title: Peter
---
<<declare $helpedPeter = false>>
<<declare $helpingPeter = false>>
<<declare $gavePeterFood = false>>

<<if $helpedPeter>>
    Peter: We can find him together!
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>

Peter: Sorry, I'm a bit busy. I can't find Stephen anywhere lately...

-> What do you mean? <<if hasActions()>>
    <<jump InquirePeter>>
-> Sorry, good luck.
    <<stop>>
===

title: InquirePeter
---
Peter: MUDA MUDA MUDA MUDA ORA ORA ORA ORA Here is some lore about Stephen.

-> Does this mean anything to you? <<if getBool("hasItem1") and hasActions() and getBool("hasItem2")>>
    <<jump helpPeter>>
-> Sorry, good luck with that.
    <<stop>>
===

title: helpPeter
---
<<useAction>>
<<set $helpedPeter = true>>
Peter: No way! This is proof that Stephen is here! Let's go!
<<stop>>
===

title: PeterClass
---
Peter is taking his notes, paying you no mind...
<<stop>>
===

title: PeterLunch
---
<<if $gavePeterFood>>
    Peter: Thanks again for the Cowfila! You saved my life!
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>

<<if $helpingPeter>>
    Peter: Hey man! Did you get that Cowfila for me yet?
    -> Yep, I got some from Greg! <<if $gotGregsFood>>
        <<jump GivePeterGregsFood>>
    -> Yep, I bought you some! <<if $boughtMeal>>
        <<jump GivePeterBoughtFood>>
    -> Not yet.
        Peter: Dang, alright. Please hurry, I'm starving!
        <<stop>>
<<else>>
    Peter: "Sniff" I'm so sad!
    -> What's wrong?
        <<jump helpPeterLunch>>
    -> Grown man btw.
        <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===

title: helpPeterLunch
---
Peter: I got hacked and have no more swipes! Now I'm gonna starve!
Peter: Wait a minute... You need chapel credits right?
Peter: If you get me some Cowfila I'll give you one of my credits! Whadda ya say?
-> Fair trade, sure.  <<if hasActions()>>
    <<jump peterLunchThanks>>
-> Nah I'm lowkey starving...
    <<jump peterDisapointed>>
===

title: peterLunchThanks
---
<<useAction>>
<<set $helpingPeter = true>>
Peter: Thanks man! Get it to me before the hour ends!
<<stop>>
===

title: GivePeterGregsFood
---
<<set $gotGregsFood = false>>
<<jump GivePeterFood>>
===

title: GivePeterBoughtFood
---
<<set $boughtMeal = false>>
<<jump GivePeterFood>>
===

title: GivePeterFood
---
<<useAction>>
Peter: NO WAY! YOU ACTUALLY GOT ME COWFILA?!
Peter: Dude, you're actually the best!
Peter: Here, take my chapel credit. A deal's a deal!

<<setBool "peterCredit" true>>
<<set $gavePeterFood = true>>
<<stop>>
===

title: peterDisapointed
---
Peter: Dang, whatever man. Good luck getting those credits...
<<stop>>
===


title: PeterCallsPlayer
---
Peter: Hey! Come over here for a second!
<<stop>>
===


title: PeterCredit
---
<<if getBool("peterCredit")>>
    Peter: Hey man, I bet you still have one more chapel credit to get, right?
    -> Yea.
        Peter: So one thing that isn't well known is that a year ago they made it so staff members also need to attend chapel, and it turns out since Opitz is the one running chapel, he technically doesn't actually have any chapel credits! He's over a year in debt! 
        -> So what?
            Peter: Well, I've been looking into Willie lately, for my own reasons... But I think what I know so far may help you.
            Peter: So you know how Willie "deals" with students who skip chapel without a chapel pass, right?
            Peter: I saw him do the same to a prof last week! If you can get evidence of Opitz not having any credits, then Willie would "deal" with him. After that, you can probably just give yourself a credit!
            -> How would I get the evidence?
                Peter: Hmmmm. I'm not entirely sure. Maybe if you can get into the classroom alone, you can find dirt on him in the desk.
                -> I'll try it, thanks.
                    Peter: Good luck, man!
<<endif>>
<<stop>>
===